  "conclusions": [
    "Not an implementation defect: extraction, labels, app grouping, native parity all consistent; failure is exactly reproducible and deterministic.",
    "Data coverage (primary): one training application (8 rows) for 8,486 parameters; normalization fitted on that application only; calibration on a second single application.",
    "Representation (contributing): geometry features mix the transferable oracle (current clip fraction) with per-app fingerprints (box position/size distributions).",
    "Calibration (proximate): a single-app absolute threshold cannot transfer when per-app score offsets (~0.3-0.7) dwarf within-app margins.",
    "Optimization (secondary): the logistic baseline failed to learn even the feature sign within 30 epochs on clip-only input (clean scored above clipped); epoch budget is insufficient at this data scale.",
    "The clip-fraction feature alone transfers perfectly (4/4 recall, 0 false positives) because it is identical across applications - it IS the deterministic measurement. For this criterion family the deterministic check remains strictly preferable; learned incremental value must be sought on harder evidence (partial clipping, other heads, automatic candidates), not by loosening thresholds.",
    "Minimum next experiment: >=5 application families (3 train + 1 calibration + 1 test) to test cross-app calibration at all; spec pilot target remains 10 families / 1,000 adjudicated regions."
  ]
